=== PARITY (vs web SignalChartPanel.tsx) ===
  Logic — faithfully ported + unit-tested:
    • useRightAxis: stats>=2; ranges = |max-min| (flat→1); right axis fires when r0/r1>10 || r1/r0>10.
    • effectiveMode: overlay→overlay; grid→(n>=2?grid:overlay); auto→(n>gridAutoThreshold(8)?grid:overlay).
    • overlay yAxis assignment: every series on the shared left scale except index 1, which (when
      useRightAxis) is rescaled onto the left domain and read back through a relabeled trailing axis
      (web `yAxisId="right"`). connectNulls = plot finite points only + monotone interpolation.
    • grid: per-cell own y-scale, finite-only projection, stride-downsample to 400 (web maxPointsPerCell).
    • header counters: live `{fmtInt(events)} events · {fmtInt(points)} points`; historical
      `{fmtInt(pointsLoaded)} points loaded` (shown only when data present and pointsLoaded != nil).
    • resolvedTitle: title override ?? (isLive ? "Live Signal Stream" : "Signal Chart").
    • isAnimationActive={!isLive} → overlay chart animation nil in live mode (also nil under Reduce Motion).
  Composition — native primitives (no Tailwind ports): TSGlassPanel (web GlassPanel), TSFadeIn (web FadeIn),
    TSChartSkeleton (web Skeleton), Swift Charts overlay (web Recharts LineChart) + a circle-dot legend
    (web `<Legend iconType="circle">`) + a synced-cursor tooltip (web ChartTooltip), and a LazyVGrid
    small-multiples grid (web SmallMultiplesChart) reusing the shared brand palette (web CHART_COLORS →
    TSChartPalette, index-stable, the same Okabe-Ito values). Recharts → Swift Charts. Leaflet → none.
  i18n — all 8 web-source strings resolve through the P1/S10 facade with the web English as the fallback:
    "Live Signal Stream", "Signal Chart", "events", "points", "points loaded",
    "Waiting for signal data…", "No data for this time range", and the grid "No data"
    (smallMultiples.noData) → ALL present in SignalChartPanel.strings. No English literals in native code.
  a11y — panel is one contained element with a localized chart summary (title + layout + signal/point
    counts); legend + tooltip rows + grid cells carry per-series labels/values; the live pulse + chart
    animation respect Reduce Motion; Dynamic Type via the token ramp. Retry button labelled.

